                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e90f90e6-e10f-3426-9046-735a4c28ea43",
                        "entry_id": "893fa770-88c5-39ff-8fe5-be78cd85f33f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто живёт, обитает где-либо (о человеке)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "60f95716-c6cd-414a-9425-2c744791a7fc",
                                "sense_id": "e90f90e6-e10f-3426-9046-735a4c28ea43",
                                "text": "Мгновение спустя — Бах знал это — каждый обитатель колонии поворачивался на звук, снимал картуз или шапку и шептал короткую молитву."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "096273b0-9b0d-3550-bf21-63bb44b1404b",
                        "entry_id": "893fa770-88c5-39ff-8fe5-be78cd85f33f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "тот, кто водится в какой-либо местности (о животном)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f55175a9-f6dd-446f-980b-7a013ce4efb1",
                                "sense_id": "096273b0-9b0d-3550-bf21-63bb44b1404b",
                                "text": "О чудесах муравьиной семьи можно рассказать ещё очень много, но вот каждый отдельный обитатель муравейника — это, как ни удивительно, просто мелкое суетливое насекомое, в действиях которого часто трудно найти какую-либо логику и цель."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0c4613c9-0b1e-4da8-ac9f-2e19e86e364c",
                        "source_entry_id": "893fa770-88c5-39ff-8fe5-be78cd85f33f",
                        "target_lang_word": "inhabitant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "inhabitant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "345c45f4-b904-3840-8217-33f3d5f10566",
                                        "entry_id": "efe7aef3-5c28-34c1-aafa-c9138b42a8c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone or thing who lives in a place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "49cdd6e6-5ae0-461b-bd6f-291622f983b2",
                                                "sense_id": "345c45f4-b904-3840-8217-33f3d5f10566",
                                                "text": "I believed it in the same way one of you might believe there are inhabitants in the planet Mars. I knew once a Scotch sailmaker who was certain, dead sure, there were people in Mars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40efea68-9e75-47f0-8bdb-dd54294a74e3",
                                                "sense_id": "345c45f4-b904-3840-8217-33f3d5f10566",
                                                "text": "It was obvious to the inhabitants of the small coastal town of Bridport that in the midst of these squabbles their need for a railway was going to be overlooked, and they decided to take the matter into their own hands."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aec6b4bb-8b01-4f91-8f55-a6f272ecb234",
                                                "sense_id": "345c45f4-b904-3840-8217-33f3d5f10566",
                                                "text": "About 98 per cent of Taiwan's inhabitants are Han Chinese, a diverse mix of ethnic and linguistic groups, including Hakka, Cantonese and Fujianese, who came from China's southern coast. Taiwan's other two per cent are from one of the nine indigenous tribes, which are scattered throughout the island but largely concentrated along the east coast and in the Central Mountain Range."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c6085fa-edd5-35db-9008-5b7c7d07af97",
                                        "entry_id": "efe7aef3-5c28-34c1-aafa-c9138b42a8c3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A possible value for a type."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c070f3b0-f6cd-4e56-b2b0-a4774281d711",
                                                "sense_id": "1c6085fa-edd5-35db-9008-5b7c7d07af97",
                                                "text": "One way to observe this connection with mathematics is by mapping each type to its cardinality, a count of the inhabitants of that type."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "inhabitant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "275a7689-faf7-3788-b72f-3e22b71c2026",
                                        "entry_id": "1faf802d-3de8-3826-8689-6fc852e298e3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "resident"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b5217ea3-6e31-4ad9-ae03-56af1691114f",
                        "source_entry_id": "893fa770-88c5-39ff-8fe5-be78cd85f33f",
                        "target_lang_word": "resident",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "resident",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7ea48e8-e0e1-3dfb-b205-3b84659efdc8",
                                        "entry_id": "a41cefbe-4b74-3871-acd2-4edb6467950f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person, animal or plant living at a certain location or in a certain area."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13d57184-0ce8-4dca-934a-d3ea2a13816e",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ea48e8-e0e1-3dfb-b205-3b84659efdc8",
                                                "text": "The tiger is a resident of the Lower Amoor, and ranges as high as 53° north latitude. In winter he roams through the same forests with the reindeer, and occasionally dines upon venison of his own catching."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aef19f30-9dd4-459d-b900-97a7257f5c63",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ea48e8-e0e1-3dfb-b205-3b84659efdc8",
                                                "text": "Mr. Cooke at once began a tirade against the residents of Asquith for permitting a sandy and generally disgraceful condition of the roads. So roundly did he vituperate the inn management in particular, and with such a loud flow of words, that I trembled lest he should be heard on the veranda."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c8136429-7771-4801-a1bd-f18c0f505726",
                                                "sense_id": "d7ea48e8-e0e1-3dfb-b205-3b84659efdc8",
                                                "text": "The acorns are more slender and pointed than the other and this tree is a resident of foothills all around the great valley up to elevations of about 3500 feet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07712543-63f0-301e-825c-829e980455c4",
                                        "entry_id": "a41cefbe-4b74-3871-acd2-4edb6467950f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bird which does not migrate during the course of the year."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a23bede-ee7c-3b1d-8a20-8d1b6285525f",
                                        "entry_id": "a41cefbe-4b74-3871-acd2-4edb6467950f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A physician receiving specialized medical training."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3e8309a-1950-4f84-a8f4-f693f3a83e78",
                                                "sense_id": "5a23bede-ee7c-3b1d-8a20-8d1b6285525f",
                                                "text": "She's a resident in neurosurgery at Mass General."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8a3bfa9-09b9-3f00-b5b6-0daa956e084b",
                                        "entry_id": "a41cefbe-4b74-3871-acd2-4edb6467950f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A diplomatic representative who resides in a foreign country, usually of inferior rank to an ambassador."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
